WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, you've worked in
Boston before --

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.069 line:92%
"Mystic River," "Patriots Day.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is it like
working in Boston

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.408 line:92%
versus other filming locales

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.209 line:92%
-Well, I love working in Boston.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.111
This is probably my sixth or
seventh thing I've done there.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:14.848
I don't really know why I keep
getting Boston gigs, but I do.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
Boston is so interesting,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:20.620 size:84% position:42%
because everybody has
a really great sense of

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
this history of the city,
but it's not just --

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.625 size:81% position:41%
It's, like, real old
historical stuff like,

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you know,
the colonials, you know,

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:28.962 line:92%
died there" or something.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't even know.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.865 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I'm not big on history.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.902
But then it's also, like,
more recent stuff, like,

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:39.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, my cousin
knows the guy that was shot.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.540 line:92%
You know, he was connected to --

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like, right in tha
alley right there."

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's --
And, so, you always get this -

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.850
It also feels like a super
super small town, you know

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.285 line:92%
Everybody knows everybody.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:55.522
Everybody knows everything
about everybody that's going on.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:58.058 line:92%
I have a great fondness for it

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:02.662
-It is true that if you ar
nice to people in Boston,

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody knows by
the next time you got back

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they all do
know each other.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yes.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.701 size:75% position:38%
-Like, I'll go back,
and they'll be like,

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.471
"Hey, my cousin Tommy worked the
door at your last show.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.440
He said you're a class act
I really appreciate it."

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, "Oh."
-Right. Right. Right.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everybody
has a friend that knows a guy.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.013 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, they do.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're very --
I want to ask about this,

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
because your first --
Not a lot of people have suc

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.320 line:92%
iconic first roles or films.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Animal House."
-Uh-huh.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were in "Animal House."
You were 18 years old.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were other people
in that movie --

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
At that point,
were they all starting out

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were there people --
Was John Belushi famous?

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.766
-John Belushi was famous because
he was on "Saturday Night Live."

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And -- Have you heard of it

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he was -- You know,
he was on "Saturday Night Live

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.611 size:75% position:38%
and also was at that
pinnacle of, like,

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
his greatness
on "Saturday night live."

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was traveling
back and forth

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "SNL," in New York,
and we were shooting

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.820 line:92%
all the way out in Oregon.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was the first real,
you know, celebrity

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I ever met --
and certainly movie star.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I was really, really,
like, taken with him,

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:13.500 size:84% position:42%
and he was a very, very
generous and warm guy.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll never forget --
he did a party

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.271 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that I got invited to.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.306 size:84% position:42%
And we were all staying
at this crappy hotel,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he had a house,
a rented house.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.511 line:92%
I think it was by the water.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.979 line:92%
And he had everybody come over

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he had brunch and he had
flown lox from New York,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that blew my mind that
first off,

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would have a party, be able
to afford it,

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:38.725 line:92%
and that they would go to --

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.393
It was, like, Zabar's,
Barney Greengrass, or something.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get this giant --
And I had ever ate lox

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.863 line:92%
because it was too expensive

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.533
-Yeah.
-And there was just piles of it.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was that combined with
the first time

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I had ever heard of
a mimosa.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:55.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this was a really, really
major point in my life.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Along with meeting John.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.712
-I mean, to be introduced to lox
and mimosas on the same day...

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. By John Belushi.
-By John Belushi. You're right

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's a lot better.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:06.886 size:84% position:42%
I think mine was, like,
my Aunt Christy. Yeah.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know her.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Cousin Christy.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thanks so much
for being here.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:16.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always such a pleasure.
Kevin Bacon, everybody.

